cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mem-Forever, please cite it as below."
title: "Mem-Forever: a Git-native persistent memory layer for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  Every AI tool forgets a user when the session closes. Mem-Forever keeps the
  memory in the user's own Git repository as small Markdown files with OKF
  frontmatter and iLang declarations that a person can read and a machine can
  parse, so preferences, decisions and lessons survive across sessions, tools
  and models. Version 2.0 turns the repository into a portable agent brain: a
  bootloader any tool reads first, a hand-off note that says what was done and
  what comes next, one file per memory, and an age-encrypted vault for keys,
  with a single-file Python tool to check, migrate and install. It needs no
  server and no account: create the repository from the template and point the
  agent at it. Version 2.1 makes the README the engineering book: copy it into
  any agent and it can carry it out; the hand-off review accepts a partial
  write-back. Documentation in nine languages.
